# template's model: `stakeOnCell` reads a per-cell `totalStake`, and `roundStep`
# was shaped around a token reserve and a board of cells.
#
# It also held a `stakeAnAvatar` written against THIS game (buy an avatar
# through the setup gate, then wait for it to be in custody). That walk is
# deleted with the rest ON PURPOSE: it was never once executed green, because
# the suite calling it failed earlier on `view.cells`, and an unverified helper
# that reads as authoritative is exactly the thing this tree keeps having to
# delete. The route it maps is worth keeping, so here it is in prose, to be
# re-derived and PROVEN when the suite is written:
#
#   the HUD's setup gate offers `buy` until the account holds an avatar;
#   `purchase.buy()` may raise a payer chooser (`purchase-payment-methods`,
#   `purchase-pay-with-<id>`), then a consent step whose button reads
#   "Sign and buy" or "Buy"; custody is then visible as
#   `context.game.deposited` going from Loaded/[] to Loaded/[one].
#
# REPLACED BY web/e2e/fixtures/board.ts, which reads this game's board (round
# step, planned actions, where the avatar is, what is in custody) and drives it
# (buy an avatar, skip the welcome overlay, plan by clicking). `stakeAnAvatar`
